<p>بِكَم <i>bikam</i> means "for how much?". Point and say بِكَم هٰذَا؟ for a masculine thing, or بِكَم هٰذِهِ؟ <i>bikam hādhihi?</i> for a feminine one, such as a bag, حَقِيبَة <i>ḥaqība</i>. The answer is a number and a currency. From eleven to ninety-nine, the currency takes -an: عِشْرُون رِيَالًا <i>ʿishrūn riyālan</i>.</p>
